### Wednesday 23 september
So the first thing we had to do today was find our groups. For the group following our efforts this should not
Be such a big problem because they already did the arduino thing together.

First we cloned the entire repository to one of our own, and added everybody as a collaborator. If you do not 
know how to do this, googling this gives a fairly straightforward guide.
Afterwards we carefully read the README.md document provided by the original explanation and looked through all files.
We noticed a couple of things:
  -  All the .step files needed to make the gearbox are already included. This means that we do **not** have to create 
     our own gears. But rather can use these files to print our first prototype.
  -  As mentioned in the README, there is a picture of the georbox under the 'results' section. We can use this to get
     a feeling for the way the gearbox should be constructed.
  -  The final goal of the project is to create a gearbox that rotates at an 8-to-50 ratio we think.
